==Trivia==
*The word "''Barbarian''" comes from the Greek "''βάρβαρος''" (''bárbaros''), meaning foreign. Dating back to the ancient Greek times, the Greeks referred to non-Greek people as barbarians because the language they spoke sounded to Greeks like gibberish represented by the sounds "''bar..bar..;''".
**In the Japanese and Thai language setting of the game, the Barbarian Barrel's name translates to "Rolling Barbarian" and "Barbarian Tank" respectively.
**The Barbarian Barrel is 1 of 6 [[cards]] associated with [[Barbarians]], with the others being [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Barbarian Launcher]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Barbarian Hut]], and of course, Barbarians.
***It is the only Barbarian-related card to be {{Rarity|Epic}}.
***It is the only Barbarian-related card to be a [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]].
***It is the only Barbarian-related card to spawn only 1 Barbarian instead of more than 1.
**According to a Clash-A-Rama comic [https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/Clash-A-Rama!_Comic_Strips?file=Barb_Barrel_ColourWeb2.jpg strip], the Barbarians follow a career path, with the one in the Barbarian Barrel being the lowest-ranking one.
*The Barbarian Barrel, along with [[Wall Breakers]], [[Rage]], and [[Goblin Curse]], are the cheapest {{Rarity|Epic}} cards, costing 2 [[Elixir]].
*The Barbarian Barrel is one of the first spell cards to receive a card render, alongside the [[Arrows]] and [[Rocket]].
*It is 1 of 3 spells that can only be placed in the player's territory, the others being [[Royal Delivery]] and [[The Log]].
*The Barbarian Barrel is 1 of 23 cards that has had its [[Elixir]] cost changed, the others being [[Bomber]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], [[Musketeer]], [[Three Musketeers]], [[Heal]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], [[Bowler]], [[Goblin Barrel]], Rage, [[Fisherman]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Barbarian Barrel is 1 of 10 cards to have an alliterative name, the others being the [[Royal Recruits]], [[Goblin Gang]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Dagger Duchess]], [[Boss Bandit]], and the [[Mighty Miner]].
*The Barbarian Barrel is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
**The Barbarian Barrel Back in Time Emote is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Back_to_the_Future Back to the Future].
*The Barbarian Barrel was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|decks]] of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Barbarian Barrel was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/cmBlEI-aDoo?si=UoD1Sit2YvQR19xs Clash Royale League 2019 Tournament], by a player called Surgical Goblin.
**The Barbarian Barrel was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/h3IOFTfT8Sk?si=wTF1FekCifpSULn- Clash Royale League 2020 Tournament], by a player called Ruben.
**The Barbarian Barrel was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/pRfrjMiHbQA?si=P2kVLJUlXH1SZoHm Clash Royale League 2021 Tournament], by a player called Mugi.
*If a [[Monk]] activates Pensive Protection in the corner of the [[Arenas|Arena]], then an opposing Barbarian Barrel will be deflected out of the Arena's bounds. However, the [[Barbarians|Barbarian]] will spawn inside the Arena.
**Thanks to the Monk, it is possible for a Barbarian Barrel to deal damage to [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Towers]] by itself. Unlike other spells, it will not deal reduced damage.
*On 3/1/2024, the Barbarian Barrel was supposed to receive a 7% damage decrease, but this change [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-55-balance-wip was pulled back last minute].

